---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How It Works"
  description="You send the buying question. I check it, research it, and send back a straight answer with the receipts."
>
  <div class="desk-page">
    <header class="desk-page-header">
      <p class="desk-eyebrow">The Buying Desk / method</p>
      <h1>Here's how it works.</h1>
      <p>
        You send the question. I check whether I can answer it. Then I research
        it and send the report. No account, dashboard, or automated checkout.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="desk-section" aria-labelledby="steps-title">
      <div class="desk-section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="desk-kicker">The sequence</p>
          <h2 id="steps-title">From question to verdict.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="desk-grid desk-process">
        <article class="desk-card">
          <h2>Build the request</h2>
          <p>
            Choose a service, describe the intended use, and include the
            relevant products, listings, budget, or deal-breakers.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="desk-card">
          <h2>Confirm scope</h2>
          <p>
            I'll reply by email with what I can check, what the report will
            cover, how long it'll take, and the price. I wont start until you
            agree.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="desk-card">
          <h2>Receive the report</h2>
          <p>
            The email report leads with the verdict, then shows evidence, risks,
            questions to ask, limitations, and confidence.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="desk-section" aria-labelledby="labels-title">
      <div class="desk-section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="desk-kicker">Evidence labels</p>
          <h2 id="labels-title">What I know and how.</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="desk-two-column">
        <article class="desk-card">
          <ul class="desk-register">
            <li>
              <strong>Personally tested</strong><span
                >I've used, built, or repaired it myself.</span
              >
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Measured research</strong><span
                >Credible documentation or independent measurement.</span
              >
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Listing information</strong><span
                >A seller or manufacturer claim that hasn’t been independently
                verified.</span
              >
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Insufficient evidence</strong><span
                >Something important is missing, so confidence drops.</span
              >
            </li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article class="desk-card">
          <h3>Remote means remote</h3>
          <p>
            A listing check isnt an inspection. Screenshots help. They still
            cant prove everything. Audio is subjective, so I'll give you useful
            buying advice instead of pretending I ran a lab.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="desk-section desk-final">
      <h2>See the finished shape.</h2>
      <p>The sample shows the answer-first report structure and its limits.</p>
      <div class="desk-actions">
        <a class="desk-button" href="/sample-report">Read the sample</a>
        <a class="desk-button secondary" href="/request">Start a request</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
